NNAAMMEE
     ppoorrttlloocckk — lock port for concurrent builds

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ppoorrttlloocckk [--gg _g_r_o_u_p] [--mm _m_o_d_e] _l_o_c_k_n_a_m_e [comment ...]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     ppoorrttlloocckk creates a lock named _l_o_c_k_n_a_m_e using open(2).  If the lock is al‐
     ready held, it will display one single wait message on stderr, sleep and
     retry until satisfaction.

     If necessary, creates the lock directory, using --mm _m_o_d_e as a mode argu‐
     ment or the default if that option is not specified, and --gg _g_r_o_u_p as the
     group owner if that option is specified.

     This implements a locking mechanism for ports building, see ‘LOCK
     INFRASTRUCTURE’ in ports(7) for details.  See also dpb(1) for a comple‐
     mentary lock infrastructure when using dpb.

